/// previously called "managed planned failovers." Aurora promotes the
/// specified secondary cluster to assume full read/write capabilities and
/// demotes the current primary cluster to a secondary (read-only) cluster,
/// maintaining the orginal replication topology. All secondary clusters are
/// synchronized with the primary at the beginning of the process so the new
/// primary continues operations for the Aurora global database without
/// losing any data. Your database is unavailable for a short time while the
/// primary and selected secondary clusters are assuming their new roles.
